.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_ATTRIBUTES 3 2026-09-10 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_attributes \- read stored per-file attributes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_attributes("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s         " "*mpq_archive",
.BI "        uint32_t               " "file_number",
.BI "        mpq_file_attributes_s " "*attributes"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Return the available stored attributes for the selected public file number.
The result has flags, crc32, filetime, md5[16], and patch_bit fields.
The file number is mapped to its physical block-table row.
.SS "Availability and Value Interpretation"
Flags identify available values; unavailable values are zero. Recognized
legacy layouts can omit rows or patch bits, so per-file availability may
differ from the archive header flags. The result is zeroed on failure.
.PP
FILETIME is an unsigned 64-bit Windows timestamp. MD5 is sixteen bytes,
not hexadecimal text. CRC32 and MD5 describe source bytes before compression;
lossy ADPCM output may not match. They are not cryptographic authentication.
The query reports stored values without verifying them.
Use \fBlibmpq__file_verify\fP() for an explicit checksum comparison.
.SS "Native Result Layout"
The native ABI is 40 bytes: fields begin at offsets 0, 4, 8, 16, and 32,
followed by reserved[4] at offset 36. Reserved bytes are returned as zero.
Natural alignment is retained; this is not the serialized little-endian payload.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns LIBMPQ_SUCCESS on success or a negative libmpq error.
EXIST means missing metadata or an invalid file number; FORMAT means
malformed attributes. I/O and allocation errors are propagated.
NULL arguments return EXIST. Use on the wrong handle type returns NOT_INITIALIZED.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__file_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_timestamp (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_finish (3)
